E2.evidence:
The crash is a null-pointer dereference in rclcpp's own implementation, reached by any caller that uses the documented default argument; the caller's use matches rclcpp's own declaration ("[inout] pruned_requests Removed requests id will be pushed to the vector if a pointer is provided."), so the mismatch is between rclcpp's documentation/default and its own code, and it would occur with any correct caller. Fix inside rclcpp: "-        pruned_requests->push_back(it->first);
+        if (pruned_requests) {
+          pruned_requests->push_back(it->first);
+        }" (https://github.com/ros2/rclcpp/pull/2008).
